WEBVTT

00:21.792 --> 00:24.688
Number 113, Hugo Coppelia.

00:25.008 --> 00:26.976
Come out. You've got a visitor.

00:31.232 --> 00:32.752
So it's you again,

00:33.360 --> 00:34.704
Noel Stollen.

00:35.312 --> 00:38.080
You've lost more weight, Hugo.

00:38.272 --> 00:39.968
You'll starve to death at this rate.

00:40.496 --> 00:41.840
What do you care?

00:42.400 --> 00:43.568
I care quite a bit.

00:44.000 --> 00:46.160
I can't have you dying on me.

00:46.496 --> 00:50.288
So you can get me out and put me on your team?

00:50.362 --> 00:51.565
Exactly!

00:53.328 --> 00:56.016
Hugo Coppelia the Puppeteer.

00:56.368 --> 01:01.198
This man awaiting his execution
as the murderer that shook the capital city

01:01.488 --> 01:04.256
was once renowned as a prodigy Seeker.

01:05.168 --> 01:09.057
Puppeteer is a rare Job
that marries combat and production,

01:09.409 --> 01:13.728
a combination you would never see otherwise.

01:14.592 --> 01:20.560
Puppeteers can fight in all kinds of situations
by controlling a variety of puppet soldiers.

01:21.296 --> 01:24.976
With his cool, collected personality
and sharp intellect,

01:25.264 --> 01:30.416
Hugo led battle after battle to victory
as a freelance Seeker.

01:32.768 --> 01:34.128
But because of that…

01:34.128 --> 01:37.856
He was a lone wolf
without anyone else on his team.

01:38.720 --> 01:42.336
Then he suddenly retired
at the peak of his career.

01:43.696 --> 01:46.960
Hugo had wanted to forge
a new path as a dollmaker,

01:47.312 --> 01:49.616
and he achieved great success in that field too.

01:50.992 --> 01:54.464
But then the incident turned his life upside down.

01:55.152 --> 01:58.352
I keep telling you, you're wasting your time.

01:58.960 --> 02:00.368
I'm going to be executed.

02:00.700 --> 02:03.744
There are plenty of ways I could go about this.

02:05.312 --> 02:08.128
You don't seem to believe me. In that case…

02:10.208 --> 02:12.240
Thank you for your patience, Noel!

02:12.544 --> 02:14.800
Thanks. You can go.

02:14.800 --> 02:15.600
Yes, sir!

02:15.600 --> 02:17.392
Let me know if you need anything!

02:19.920 --> 02:21.328
Quality tea.

02:21.776 --> 02:24.112
You bought the guards?

02:24.464 --> 02:27.824
Oh, I just know a little weakness of his.

02:28.256 --> 02:30.080
You threatened him…?

02:30.167 --> 02:32.080
I'll leave it to your imagination.

02:32.464 --> 02:37.392
Let's just say that any guard
in this prison would listen to me.

02:38.816 --> 02:40.112
I'm serious.

02:40.688 --> 02:43.984
The groundwork is being laid to free you.

02:45.904 --> 02:48.464
What's wrong? Aren't you happy?

02:49.392 --> 02:53.968
I would certainly be glad if I could
actually get out of here.

02:54.643 --> 02:56.976
But I can't join you.

02:57.264 --> 02:58.016
Why not?

02:59.280 --> 03:02.432
Because I can't stand Seekers.

03:02.816 --> 03:07.552
They're all violent idiots
who exaggerate their combat prowess.

03:07.888 --> 03:09.696
Are you saying I'm like that?

03:10.240 --> 03:13.216
No. You're not like the others in a bad way.

03:13.216 --> 03:15.888
You're like a snake.

03:16.432 --> 03:18.336
You're cunning and merciless.

03:18.336 --> 03:21.344
You deceive people only to swallow them whole.

03:21.712 --> 03:24.400
I've gotten that before.

03:24.912 --> 03:26.672
Not a bad compliment.

03:27.323 --> 03:29.936
It made it easy to choose a clan name.

03:30.496 --> 03:32.416
It wasn't a compliment.

03:33.584 --> 03:34.432
I'll be back.

03:34.752 --> 03:37.232
I'm persistent like a snake, you see.

03:39.616 --> 03:41.264
Hugo Coppelia.

03:42.128 --> 03:45.808
You'll join my team. I'll make sure of it.

03:52.304 --> 03:55.024
I'll be a Seeker again…?

05:28.064 --> 05:29.696
We're going to a new bar from now on.

05:30.720 --> 05:32.912
The Rock-Hard Beak?

05:33.120 --> 05:34.479
Is the food good?

05:34.590 --> 05:39.728
Hold on. Isn't that bar for
B-Rank Seekers and above?

05:39.728 --> 05:40.848
Noel?!

05:50.864 --> 05:52.848
Haven't seen you around, miss.

05:53.392 --> 05:56.544
I'm not a miss. I'm a man.

05:56.912 --> 06:02.432
Ha, you call yourself a man with
that pretty face without any battle scars?

06:02.512 --> 06:04.816
Scars make you a man?

06:05.120 --> 06:09.664
Then you must have wanted
to be a man really badly, miss.

06:09.664 --> 06:11.664
What'd you just…?!

06:11.968 --> 06:15.360
Are you going to fight all of us alone, Edgar?

06:15.696 --> 06:18.624
I see how you're the raid captain of War Eagle.

06:19.580 --> 06:24.416
You think just because you know of me,
you know exactly how to deal with me?

06:24.416 --> 06:26.128
Bruno if it's a boy.

06:26.512 --> 06:28.416
Catua if it's a girl.

06:29.920 --> 06:34.512
I hear the baby's due soon. Congratulations.

06:34.512 --> 06:36.424
How do you…

06:36.488 --> 06:38.056
Trade secret.

06:38.832 --> 06:41.104
But if you want to fight me…

06:41.104 --> 06:43.808
You'll risk everything you have.

06:44.224 --> 06:46.736
Are you ready to do that?

06:50.432 --> 06:52.656
Thanks for the warm welcome, Edgar!

06:52.944 --> 06:57.552
I'm Talker Noel Stollen, leader of Blue Beyond.

06:58.256 --> 07:00.112
Glad to make your acquaintance!

07:02.160 --> 07:03.792
Mm, yummy!

07:04.000 --> 07:06.032
They've got liquor from my country!

07:06.032 --> 07:08.032
Don't get too excited.

07:08.640 --> 07:12.640
We're not here just to eat and drink.

07:13.408 --> 07:15.296
Our real objective is…

07:16.672 --> 07:19.984
Lucky. On the very first visit.

07:21.536 --> 07:22.768
I'm surprised.

07:23.056 --> 07:25.856
I thought you were a rookie, Alma.

07:26.000 --> 07:27.232
You know each other?

07:27.616 --> 07:29.344
She knows Lycia.

07:29.344 --> 07:31.216
I only met her once.

07:31.696 --> 07:33.360
But watch out.

07:33.360 --> 07:36.176
That elf doesn't like you very much.

07:36.384 --> 07:38.048
That's great.

07:38.848 --> 07:40.848
Let's fight, then.

07:42.544 --> 07:46.528
You're awful, Noel. But I don't
hate that about you.

07:47.216 --> 07:48.640
Hi, Ophelia.

07:49.024 --> 07:51.504
Um, those two are…?

07:51.504 --> 07:52.880
My teammates.

07:53.904 --> 07:56.800
I'm Noel Stollen of Blue Beyond.

07:57.072 --> 07:58.544
What?!

07:59.280 --> 08:01.296
Ooh, scary face.

08:01.296 --> 08:03.296
Got something to say to me?

08:03.680 --> 08:07.760
How can you act like that
after selling your friends as slaves?!

08:07.948 --> 08:09.760
Oh, that?

08:10.280 --> 08:12.584
I got a good price for them from the mob.

08:13.392 --> 08:16.944
Aren't friends great to have around?

08:17.024 --> 08:18.608
You…!

08:19.280 --> 08:22.096
Don't get rough, Miss Elf.

08:22.672 --> 08:25.984
Noel's my valued master.

08:26.384 --> 08:29.408
You'll have to get through me
if you want to touch him.

08:30.192 --> 08:31.856
What a loyal dog.

08:32.288 --> 08:34.864
Wagging your tail for a leader
that sells his party members.

08:35.537 --> 08:38.577
Say all you want about me.

08:39.180 --> 08:40.080
But…

08:40.969 --> 08:43.753
You should choose your words carefully.

08:44.288 --> 08:46.809
Don't make me draw my sword.

08:48.800 --> 08:50.624
What's wrong, Ophelia?

08:51.040 --> 08:55.376
Your member here tried to grab me out of nowhere.

08:56.144 --> 08:57.280
Is that true?

08:57.872 --> 08:58.992
Sorry…

08:59.760 --> 09:00.672
I see…

09:03.824 --> 09:06.640
What my member did wasn't right.

09:07.360 --> 09:08.032
I'm sorry.

09:08.496 --> 09:10.016
It's no big deal.

09:10.560 --> 09:13.392
Just train her so it doesn't happen again.

09:14.000 --> 09:16.560
Even dogs can be trained not to attack people.

09:16.976 --> 09:18.928
Your member's dumber than a dog.

09:20.816 --> 09:21.840
Dumber than a dog?

09:22.704 --> 09:25.264
I might have to make you take that back.

09:25.712 --> 09:27.344
Taking the offensive?

09:27.600 --> 09:32.528
I apologize for Ophelia's rudeness,
but that doesn't make it okay to insult her.

09:32.992 --> 09:36.544
So you want to make it out
like we're both at fault.

09:37.120 --> 09:38.480
You're a strategist.

09:39.808 --> 09:42.464
You can't talk to him in good faith, Leon.

09:42.464 --> 09:45.408
This is that Noel Stollen I told you about!

09:46.480 --> 09:47.568
You're…

09:48.192 --> 09:50.816
All the rumors were true.

09:51.424 --> 09:53.600
So I couldn't restrain myself…

09:54.064 --> 09:56.992
You like gossip? How girly of you.

09:57.536 --> 10:00.624
Do you like to play house on the side?

10:01.152 --> 10:03.216
Perhaps dolls too?

10:04.800 --> 10:06.896
You're vile.

10:07.105 --> 10:10.593
A man who can't treat his party members
with respect isn't qualified to be a Seeker.

10:10.928 --> 10:13.808
I already have the qualifications.

10:14.624 --> 10:17.648
Are you saying I need your approval?

10:18.144 --> 10:24.032
So the Winged Knights are so high and mighty
that you have input on what the Seeker Guild does?

10:24.688 --> 10:28.576
You can keep living your life
insulting people like that.

10:28.864 --> 10:30.896
But it'll come back to bite you someday.

10:31.296 --> 10:34.736
Oh, so now you're God?

10:35.184 --> 10:36.864
Aren't you arrogant?

10:37.264 --> 10:39.264
You think you're always right, huh?

10:39.616 --> 10:42.112
Well, that'll come back to bite you.

10:44.368 --> 10:45.392
Leon.

10:56.881 --> 10:58.945
Noel's the villain, confirmed.

10:59.232 --> 11:01.760
Didn't you go too far there?

11:01.984 --> 11:05.020
He was genuinely apologizing. Why'd you have to…

11:05.056 --> 11:07.744
It's okay. It's part of my plan.

11:08.912 --> 11:10.336
Listen for a second.

11:13.040 --> 11:13.904
That's dirty!

11:14.848 --> 11:17.200
Here's a lesson for you.

11:17.584 --> 11:20.080
It's eat or be eaten in the Seeker world.

11:20.864 --> 11:23.296
But it's not the weak that get eaten.

11:23.840 --> 11:27.856
It's the ones that get cocky.

11:28.512 --> 11:32.288
The ones that let their enemies see their backs.

11:32.608 --> 11:34.736
It's like asking to be killed.

11:35.184 --> 11:40.304
They're going to be our stepping stones.

11:41.680 --> 11:44.576
Hey, who's your favorite, gramps?

11:44.880 --> 11:48.896
Marion… Have some manners.

11:49.312 --> 11:53.880
This is a workplace, and I'm your senior.

11:53.968 --> 11:55.664
Oh, shut up.

11:55.786 --> 11:57.760
What's your answer?

11:57.888 --> 12:02.416
Who'd be best to command the battle
against the Valiant?

12:02.912 --> 12:06.016
Who do you think, Marion?

12:06.768 --> 12:08.976
I'd have to go with Leo Edin.

12:09.376 --> 12:13.664
And I'm not just saying that because
I'm in charge of Pandemonium.

12:13.920 --> 12:16.960
Leo's an arrogant, lazy bastard.

12:17.184 --> 12:19.216
But nobody can beat his power.

12:19.216 --> 12:21.920
He's gotta be the strongest in all of history.

12:22.288 --> 12:23.388
I see.

12:23.472 --> 12:26.490
What? Are you for Supreme Dragon?

12:27.040 --> 12:30.224
I mean, Zeke Feinstein's definitely strong, but…

12:31.120 --> 12:34.032
I think it should be Noel Stollen.

12:34.474 --> 12:35.106
Huh?

12:37.200 --> 12:38.464
No way!

12:38.464 --> 12:42.192
You're the one who turned down
his clan application! How can you say that?

12:42.192 --> 12:43.952
Would you like to bet?

12:44.384 --> 12:44.944
Huh?

12:45.616 --> 12:49.520
Leo or Noel. Who will be the commander?

12:49.920 --> 12:55.936
If you win, you can be head of the Jenkins family.

12:55.936 --> 12:57.776
But if you lose…

12:57.776 --> 13:00.816
I have to go to etiquette school?

13:00.816 --> 13:02.816
Yes, that will do.

13:03.104 --> 13:08.320
A great inspector needs
both knowledge and grace, Marion.

13:10.144 --> 13:12.720
What do you say? If you're afraid to lose…

13:12.720 --> 13:14.416
Hell no!

13:14.576 --> 13:17.472
All right! It's a bet!

13:20.128 --> 13:25.560
Don't disappoint me, Noel Stollen.

13:28.016 --> 13:30.970
[X - The Haves and the Have-Nots]

13:35.152 --> 13:38.688
- We got this!
- Let's go! Our future is bright!

13:39.785 --> 13:40.817
Jeez.

13:41.776 --> 13:43.472
What a handful.

13:44.144 --> 13:45.808
You goody-two-shoes!

13:46.208 --> 13:48.752
That's what you get for snitching!

13:49.104 --> 13:53.600
But… taking stuff from shops is stealing.

13:53.904 --> 13:54.848
Shut up!

13:54.848 --> 13:56.848
It doesn't make a difference!

13:56.848 --> 13:58.848
You're so annoying!

13:58.848 --> 14:01.712
But it's wrong. You shouldn't do it.

14:01.744 --> 14:04.432
Huh? Are you God or something?!

14:05.376 --> 14:08.000
Hey! What're you doing?!

14:08.592 --> 14:10.080
Crap, it's Keim!

14:10.080 --> 14:10.784
Run!

14:13.360 --> 14:15.232
So they got you again, Leon.

14:16.480 --> 14:18.432
You should fight back.

14:18.432 --> 14:19.600
I can't.

14:19.872 --> 14:24.048
Didn't you just find out
you have a combat-type Job?

14:24.240 --> 14:26.432
You could easily…

14:26.432 --> 14:29.488
You shouldn't respond
to violence with violence, Keim.

14:30.128 --> 14:31.408
It isn't right.

14:31.712 --> 14:35.056
All this talk of what is and isn't right.

14:39.872 --> 14:43.184
It's always the same with you.

14:44.976 --> 14:48.080
Hey, Leon. Let's be Seekers.

14:48.336 --> 14:48.928
Huh?

14:49.872 --> 14:52.624
It wouldn't be any use staying
in this backwater town.

14:53.008 --> 14:55.280
I want to see the world.

14:55.824 --> 14:59.824
I think we could be the best Seekers ever!

15:00.496 --> 15:02.224
I couldn't.

15:02.752 --> 15:04.800
I'm not strong like you, Keim.

15:05.248 --> 15:07.824
No, you're strong, Leon.

15:09.328 --> 15:12.160
You're a Swordsman. I'm a Lancer.

15:12.400 --> 15:14.144
We're not like the others.

15:14.720 --> 15:16.480
We have it.

15:16.896 --> 15:17.936
But…

15:17.936 --> 15:19.744
We're gonna be Seekers!

15:20.080 --> 15:23.296
When we grow up, we'll be cool
and do the right thing!

15:24.272 --> 15:26.416
Do… the right thing?

15:26.672 --> 15:29.824
Yeah. We'll protect everyone
by getting rid of beasts.

15:30.000 --> 15:32.416
What could be more right than that?

15:35.776 --> 15:39.984
I was drawn to him ever since we were kids.

15:41.200 --> 15:43.472
Because he has something I don't?

15:43.840 --> 15:46.848
No. I wasn't thinking back then.

15:47.840 --> 15:50.464
I just wanted to be someone.

15:54.240 --> 15:55.392
Now, Leon!

15:55.632 --> 15:57.648
Use Seraphim Blade!

15:57.648 --> 16:00.304
I can't! It'll hit you at this range!

16:00.304 --> 16:02.544
I'll dodge as soon as you use it!

16:02.544 --> 16:04.352
It's the only way we can win!

16:06.448 --> 16:09.440
You can do it! Believe in me, Leon!

16:17.856 --> 16:20.208
Seraphim Blade!

16:26.480 --> 16:27.872
W-We won…

16:28.432 --> 16:30.336
We won!

16:30.560 --> 16:33.696
The Depth-7 forest dragon, Aiatar…

16:34.144 --> 16:36.800
To think we've come this far.

16:38.960 --> 16:41.408
Keim! Are you okay?

16:43.728 --> 16:45.360
What's that look for?

16:46.352 --> 16:48.288
We won.

16:48.752 --> 16:51.680
This'll move Twilight Glint up in the world.

16:51.680 --> 16:52.384
Yeah.

16:53.184 --> 16:58.240
Twilight Glint was the party name
the four of us chose.

16:59.200 --> 17:01.568
But that name never caught on.

17:02.800 --> 17:09.856
People started calling us the Winged Knights
after Leon's special Angel Wings ability.

17:11.216 --> 17:13.280
Leon was the one who had it.

17:13.696 --> 17:16.944
The one who could be somebody.

17:21.104 --> 17:24.000
So why'd you get so heated?

17:24.288 --> 17:25.872
I'm not sure.

17:26.144 --> 17:28.128
I don't really get it myself.

17:29.008 --> 17:30.256
Were you jealous?

17:30.656 --> 17:31.632
Jealous?

17:32.160 --> 17:38.400
Yeah. Some kid that just became a Seeker
showed up at the Rock-Hard Beak.

17:38.816 --> 17:40.864
Acting like he's someone important.

17:43.127 --> 17:46.576
How many years did it take us
to get into that place?

17:46.960 --> 17:48.992
Of course you'd be jealous.

17:49.904 --> 17:52.384
I don't blame Ophelia for snapping either.

17:53.120 --> 17:55.648
I see… Jealousy.

17:56.560 --> 18:00.880
I can't believe I didn't realize how I felt.

18:02.768 --> 18:05.248
Yeah. He's impressive.

18:05.600 --> 18:10.048
I can't agree with how he does things,
but his hard work deserves respect.

18:12.320 --> 18:15.632
Leon, integrity is a virtue.

18:16.016 --> 18:19.392
But I don't know about
just letting them surpass us.

18:20.688 --> 18:23.184
I got this from the Seeker Guild.

18:23.616 --> 18:28.304
It says that skilled parties should
form clans as soon as possible.

18:28.512 --> 18:31.312
Ophelia and Vaclav got the same letter.

18:31.680 --> 18:35.424
Really? I actually got one too.

18:36.288 --> 18:40.336
I actually invited you
to the tavern to discuss it.

18:41.808 --> 18:43.920
But then that happened…

18:45.344 --> 18:49.280
Oh. Well, the other two say
they'll defer to your decision.

18:49.744 --> 18:51.088
So will I, of course.

18:51.872 --> 18:55.248
You've already talked about it? Without me?

18:55.648 --> 18:57.216
It saved us time, right?

18:59.328 --> 19:01.600
I know I'm just leader for show, but…

19:01.600 --> 19:03.213
Don't sulk!

19:03.214 --> 19:06.176
Your image is vital to us.

19:07.040 --> 19:08.400
For our future…

19:09.136 --> 19:10.656
For forming a clan.

19:14.560 --> 19:16.112
Application rejected?

19:16.880 --> 19:17.776
Why?

19:18.320 --> 19:20.528
All the documents were in order.

19:20.704 --> 19:22.432
And we meet the requirements.

19:22.432 --> 19:25.136
Yes, there was no issue there.

19:25.584 --> 19:29.872
We would have happily
accepted you at any other time.

19:29.872 --> 19:31.184
So why…

19:34.016 --> 19:37.440
A Valiant is appearing. In a year's time…

19:37.744 --> 19:42.656
That's why we need people
who can fight immediately.

19:42.992 --> 19:44.960
Then there should be no problem.

19:44.960 --> 19:48.528
We successfully defeated an Aiatar.

19:48.688 --> 19:50.720
If we're dragon-killers…

19:50.720 --> 19:55.008
Then why didn't you apply
to be a clan right afterward?

19:56.144 --> 19:58.672
The issue is that seriousness.

19:58.880 --> 20:01.504
That hunger to always climb higher.

20:01.504 --> 20:03.984
That's lacking in you.

20:04.432 --> 20:05.840
But…

20:06.784 --> 20:09.200
Then what's this letter about?

20:09.328 --> 20:13.248
I don't recall sending out such letters.

20:13.504 --> 20:14.704
It must be a hoax.

20:16.400 --> 20:20.688
A hoax? But who… And why?

20:21.008 --> 20:23.168
Well, that concludes our interview.

20:23.408 --> 20:26.065
Thank you for your time.

20:26.144 --> 20:29.536
Wait! Please give us another chance!

20:29.840 --> 20:31.056
Please!

20:33.248 --> 20:36.320
Alright. You can have another chance.

20:36.608 --> 20:37.776
Really?!

20:38.192 --> 20:42.512
Yes. I'd just like you to undergo a test.

20:42.768 --> 20:43.664
A test?

20:44.096 --> 20:47.488
To defeat a specified beast.

20:47.632 --> 20:50.976
I'll acknowledge you as a clan if you can do that.

20:51.712 --> 20:53.312
What beast?

20:54.480 --> 20:58.512
The mind-reading Dantalion of Abyssal Depth 8.

20:59.552 --> 21:04.288
It's a stronger beast than the Depth-7 Aiatar.

21:06.400 --> 21:07.664
Don't hesitate, Leon.

21:07.872 --> 21:11.040
We'd have fought it eventually as Seekers.

21:11.328 --> 21:13.648
This just means we'll do it sooner.

21:14.448 --> 21:16.288
Yeah. You're right.

21:16.832 --> 21:20.448
Okay. I accept the test.

21:20.448 --> 21:22.080
Understood.

21:22.656 --> 21:25.792
However, this test will be a competition.

21:26.400 --> 21:30.560
There's another party
whose clan application I denied.

